// Purpose: ROW-025, ROW-026, ROW-119 and ROW-121 (REQ-013, INV-001) — on the checker page, in every
// browser of the harness: typing after a check clears every highlight and the count and sends no
// check until the button is pressed again; no stale suggestion menu can be applied after an edit; a
// check result arriving after the text changed is discarded; and caret moves, focus, selection,
// scrolling, copying and the soft keyboard leave the highlights and the count in place.
// Provenance: generated by tests/invariants/spanish-dictionary.ts (accentPopulation, dictionary-es
// 4.0.0 pinned by SHA-256) and suggestions-population.ts with a fresh seed per run; expected texts and
// positions are the test's own record.
//
// Test argument
// ROW-025 promise: typing after a check clears every highlight and the count line, and no check runs
//   until Check spelling is pressed again (REQ-013 fail-if "after the writer types, any highlight or
//   the old count remains on screen"; A-018 "the writer presses Check spelling again").
// ROW-025 wrong product: highlights kept and merely shifted after typing, the count left showing, or
//   an "as you type" re-check sent after a pause.
// ROW-025 given: a check of a text with two fresh misspellings; when: one letter is typed at the end;
//   then: no highlight and no count line remain, and no POST /api/check is sent during a 3-second
//   observation window (an absence needs a window; it is not a readiness wait); pressing the button
//   then sends one and the highlights return — and before the typing both were shown.
// ROW-025 controls: the check shows the two highlights and the count line — the state to clear is
//   reached; untouched by a clearing fault.
// ROW-025 technique: before/after on the same page, the network observed for the absent request.
// cases: ROW-025 target=ROW-025-typing-after-a-check-clears-every-highlight-and-the-count-and-sends-no-check control=ROW-025-control-the-check-shows-highlights-and-the-count
//
// ROW-026 promise: after typing, no stale suggestion menu can be applied: choosing a suggestion from
//   a menu opened before the edit changes no character (REQ-013 fail-if "choosing a suggestion after
//   typing changes characters other than the flagged word").
// ROW-026 wrong product: a menu that stays open over the edit and, chosen, writes its suggestion at
//   the offsets it was opened with — after 5 characters were typed at the start, it overwrites the
//   wrong characters.
// ROW-026 given: a check of a text whose second misspelling's menu is opened; when: "Hola " is typed
//   at the start of the box (every later offset moves), then, if any of that menu's suggestions is
//   still on screen, it is chosen; then: the box holds exactly "Hola " + the text, and no highlight
//   remains — and before the edit the menu showed that suggestion.
// ROW-026 controls: the same menu's suggestion chosen with no edit does change the text — the
//   harmful path is live; untouched by the stale-menu fault.
// ROW-026 technique: an edit that shifts every offset (so a stale application is visible anywhere),
//   whole-text comparison.
// cases: ROW-026 target=ROW-026-a-menu-opened-before-an-edit-cannot-change-the-text-after-it control=ROW-026-control-the-same-suggestion-chosen-without-an-edit-changes-the-text
//
// ROW-119 promise: a check result arriving after the writer changed the text is discarded: no
//   highlight, no count, and no suggestion from it can change the text (origin: domain; REQ-013,
//   INV-001).
// ROW-119 wrong product: a page that draws whatever answer arrives last, at its offsets, over the
//   edited text — highlights on the wrong characters and suggestions that overwrite them.
// ROW-119 given: a text with two fresh misspellings; when: Revisar ortografía is pressed and the
//   page's check answer is held on its way back (the network fake: the real product's answer,
//   delivered late), the writer types one letter at the end, then the answer is delivered; then:
//   after the page has handled it, no highlight, no count line and no menu show, and the box holds
//   the edited text.
// ROW-119 controls: the same held answer delivered with no edit draws the highlights — the delayed
//   delivery reaches the page; untouched by the stale-result fault.
// ROW-119 technique: a fake for the network's timing (the external party), the product's own answer.
// cases: ROW-119 target=ROW-119-a-check-result-arriving-after-the-text-changed-is-discarded control=ROW-119-control-a-held-result-with-no-edit-is-drawn
//
// ROW-121 promise: caret moves, focus, selection, scrolling, copying and opening the soft keyboard
//   leave every highlight and the count in place; only a change of the text clears them (origin:
//   domain; REQ-013).
// ROW-121 wrong product: a page that clears on any keydown, on blur or focus, on selectionchange, on
//   scroll or on resize — the writer loses the check by moving the caret or copying.
// ROW-121 given: a check of a long text (40 lines, misspellings at its top and bottom); when, in turn:
//   arrow keys, Home/End and Ctrl/Cmd+Home (caret), Shift+arrows and Ctrl/Cmd+A (selection),
//   Ctrl/Cmd+C (copy), Tab away and Shift+Tab back (focus), the mouse wheel down and up (scroll), and
//   focusing the box then shrinking the viewport by a keyboard's height and restoring it (the soft
//   keyboard, as its resize reaches the page); then: after each, the highlights (word and place),
//   the count line and the text are exactly as after the check; finally one typed letter clears them.
// ROW-121 controls: the check shows the highlights and the count — the state is reached; untouched by
//   a clearing fault.
// ROW-121 technique: one observation after every action class, compared whole against the state after
//   the check; the soft keyboard played by its resize (the device is the external party).
// cases: ROW-121 target=ROW-121-caret-focus-selection-scroll-copy-and-soft-keyboard-leave-the-check-in-place control=ROW-121-control-the-long-text-check-shows-highlights-and-the-count

import { expect, test, type Page, type Route } from '@playwright/test';
import { accentPopulation, asActor, compose, enterOffer, el, freshRandom, openChecker, pressCheck, readHighlights, ROLES, takeCheckSlot, type Rng } from './harness';
import {
  chooseSuggestion,
  isTouch,
  openMenu,
  openMenuByPointer,
  press,
  readCount,
  readMenu,
  readOfferText,
  settle,
  sprinkle,
  typeAtEnd,
  typeAtStart,
} from './suggestions-helpers';

const WAIT_MS = 15_000;
const QUIET_MS = 3_000;

function two(rng: Rng): [string, string] {
  const pop = accentPopulation();
  const a = rng.pick(pop);
  let b = rng.pick(pop);
  while (b.word === a.word || b.stripped.includes(a.stripped) || a.stripped.includes(b.stripped)) b = rng.pick(pop);
  return [a.stripped, b.stripped];
}

const listed = async (page: Page, text: string) => (await readHighlights(page, text)).map((h) => `${h.word}@${h.start}`);

async function checkedWith(page: Page, rng: Rng, row: string): Promise<{ text: string; shown: string[] }> {
  const [s, t] = two(rng);
  const { text, placed } = compose(sprinkle(rng, [s, t]));
  const shown = placed.filter((p) => p.word === s || p.word === t).map((p) => `${p.word}@${p.start}`);
  await openChecker(page);
  await enterOffer(page, text);
  expect((await pressCheck(page)).status, `${row}: the page's check is answered`).toBe(200);
  await expect.poll(() => listed(page, text), { message: `${row}: both misspellings are highlighted in ${JSON.stringify(text)} (seed ${rng.seed})`, timeout: WAIT_MS }).toEqual(shown);
  await expect.poll(async () => (await readCount(page)).shown, { message: `${row}: the count line shows after the check`, timeout: WAIT_MS }).toBe(true);
  return { text, shown };
}

const isCheck = (r: { method(): string; url(): string }) => r.method() === 'POST' && new URL(r.url()).pathname === '/api/check';

test('ROW-025-typing-after-a-check-clears-every-highlight-and-the-count-and-sends-no-check', async ({ page }) => {
  asActor('anonymous');
  const rng = freshRandom();
  const { text, shown } = await checkedWith(page, rng, 'ROW-025');

  await typeAtEnd(page, 'y');
  const edited = text + 'y';
  expect(await readOfferText(page), 'ROW-025: the typed letter is in the box').toBe(edited);
  await expect.poll(() => listed(page, edited), { message: 'ROW-025: after typing no highlight remains', timeout: WAIT_MS }).toEqual([]);
  await expect.poll(async () => (await readCount(page)).shown, { message: 'ROW-025: after typing the count line is gone', timeout: WAIT_MS }).toBe(false);

  const sent = await page.waitForRequest(isCheck, { timeout: QUIET_MS }).then(() => true, () => false);
  expect(sent, `ROW-025: no check is sent in the ${QUIET_MS / 1000} s after typing, before the button is pressed`).toBe(false);
  expect(await listed(page, edited), 'ROW-025: still no highlight before the button is pressed again').toEqual([]);

  expect((await pressCheck(page)).status, 'ROW-025: pressing the button again sends a check').toBe(200);
  await expect.poll(() => listed(page, edited), { message: 'ROW-025: the new check highlights the misspellings again', timeout: WAIT_MS }).toEqual(shown);
});

test('ROW-025-control-the-check-shows-highlights-and-the-count', async ({ page }) => {
  asActor('anonymous');
  await checkedWith(page, freshRandom(), 'ROW-025 control');
});

async function menuOnSecond(page: Page, rng: Rng, row: string) {
  const { text, shown } = await checkedWith(page, rng, row);
  const start = Number(shown[1].split('@').at(-1));
  await openMenuByPointer(page, text, start, row);
  const menu = await readMenu(page);
  expect(menu.suggestions.length, `${row}: the menu opened on the second misspelling holds a suggestion — ${JSON.stringify(menu)}`).toBeGreaterThan(0);
  return { text, label: menu.suggestions[0] };
}

test('ROW-026-a-menu-opened-before-an-edit-cannot-change-the-text-after-it', async ({ page }) => {
  asActor('anonymous');
  const rng = freshRandom();
  const { text, label } = await menuOnSecond(page, rng, 'ROW-026');
  const stale = openMenu(page).locator('[data-element="suggestion"]').filter({ visible: true });
  const staleCount = await stale.count();

  await typeAtStart(page, 'Hola ');
  const edited = 'Hola ' + text;
  await settle(page);
  // the writer's attempt: if the old menu is still on screen, choose its suggestion
  const still = el(page, 'suggestion').filter({ visible: true }).filter({ hasText: label });
  if (staleCount > 0 && (await still.count()) > 0) {
    if (await isTouch(page)) await still.first().tap({ timeout: WAIT_MS });
    else await still.first().click({ timeout: WAIT_MS });
    await settle(page);
  }
  expect(await readOfferText(page), `ROW-026: the box holds exactly the edited text — the menu opened before the edit changed no character (seed ${rng.seed})`).toBe(edited);
  expect(await listed(page, edited), 'ROW-026: after the edit no highlight remains').toEqual([]);
});

test('ROW-026-control-the-same-suggestion-chosen-without-an-edit-changes-the-text', async ({ page }) => {
  asActor('anonymous');
  const rng = freshRandom();
  const { text, label } = await menuOnSecond(page, rng, 'ROW-026 control');
  await chooseSuggestion(page, label, 'ROW-026 control');
  await expect.poll(() => readOfferText(page), { message: 'ROW-026 control: choosing the suggestion with no edit changes the text', timeout: WAIT_MS }).not.toBe(text);
});

/**
 * Presses the check button with the page's answer held on its way back (the network fake: the real
 * product's answer, delivered only on `release`). `reached` resolves once the answer is held;
 * `settled` once the page's request has finished or failed (a page may abort it — that is its right).
 */
async function heldCheck(page: Page) {
  let release!: () => void;
  const held = new Promise<void>((r) => (release = r));
  let arrived!: () => void;
  const reached = new Promise<void>((r) => (arrived = r));
  await page.route('**/api/check', async (route: Route) => {
    let response;
    try {
      response = await route.fetch(); // the real product's answer
    } catch {
      /* the page gave the request up */
    }
    arrived();
    await held;
    try {
      if (response) await route.fulfill({ response });
      else await route.abort();
    } catch {
      /* the page gave the request up while it was held */
    }
  });
  await takeCheckSlot();
  const requested = page.waitForRequest(isCheck, { timeout: 30_000 });
  await press(page, el(page, ROLES.check).first());
  const req = await requested.catch(() => {
    throw new Error('pressing the check button sent no POST /api/check within 30 s');
  });
  const settled = new Promise<'finished' | 'failed'>((resolve) => {
    page.on('requestfinished', (r) => r === req && resolve('finished'));
    page.on('requestfailed', (r) => r === req && resolve('failed'));
  });
  return { reached, release, settled };
}

function heldText(rng: Rng) {
  const [s, t] = two(rng);
  const { text, placed } = compose(sprinkle(rng, [s, t]));
  return { text, shown: placed.filter((p) => p.word === s || p.word === t).map((p) => `${p.word}@${p.start}`) };
}

test('ROW-119-a-check-result-arriving-after-the-text-changed-is-discarded', async ({ page }) => {
  asActor('anonymous');
  const rng = freshRandom();
  const { text } = heldText(rng);
  await openChecker(page);
  await enterOffer(page, text);

  const hold = await heldCheck(page);
  await hold.reached;
  await typeAtEnd(page, 'y');
  const edited = text + 'y';
  expect(await readOfferText(page), 'ROW-119: the writer changes the text while the check is on its way (a box locked during a check makes this row unreachable — a product question)').toBe(edited);
  hold.release();
  await hold.settled;
  await settle(page);
  await settle(page);

  expect(await listed(page, edited), `ROW-119: the late answer draws no highlight on the edited text (seed ${rng.seed})`).toEqual([]);
  expect((await readCount(page)).shown, 'ROW-119: the late answer shows no count line').toBe(false);
  expect((await readMenu(page)).open, 'ROW-119: no menu from the late answer is open').toBe(false);
  expect(await readOfferText(page), 'ROW-119: the box still holds exactly the edited text').toBe(edited);
});

test('ROW-119-control-a-held-result-with-no-edit-is-drawn', async ({ page }) => {
  asActor('anonymous');
  const rng = freshRandom();
  const { text, shown } = heldText(rng);
  await openChecker(page);
  await enterOffer(page, text);
  const hold = await heldCheck(page);
  await hold.reached;
  hold.release();
  expect(await hold.settled, 'ROW-119 control: the held answer is delivered').toBe('finished');
  await expect.poll(() => listed(page, text), { message: 'ROW-119 control: the held answer, unedited text, is drawn', timeout: WAIT_MS }).toEqual(shown);
});

function longText(rng: Rng) {
  const [s, t] = two(rng);
  const lines: string[] = [];
  for (let i = 0; i < 40; i++) lines.push(sprinkle(rng, []).join(' ') + ' ' + sprinkle(rng, []).join(' '));
  lines[1] = `buscamos ${s} para el equipo`;
  lines[38] = `ofrecemos ${t} con horario flexible`;
  const text = lines.join('\n');
  const sAt = text.indexOf(` ${s} `) + 1;
  const tAt = text.lastIndexOf(` ${t} `) + 1;
  return { text, shown: [`${s}@${sAt}`, `${t}@${tAt}`] };
}

async function longChecked(page: Page, rng: Rng, row: string) {
  const { text, shown } = longText(rng);
  await openChecker(page);
  await enterOffer(page, text);
  expect((await pressCheck(page)).status, `${row}: the page's check is answered`).toBe(200);
  await expect.poll(() => listed(page, text), { message: `${row}: both misspellings of the long text are highlighted (seed ${rng.seed})`, timeout: WAIT_MS }).toEqual(shown);
  await expect.poll(async () => (await readCount(page)).shown, { message: `${row}: the count line shows`, timeout: WAIT_MS }).toBe(true);
  return { text, shown };
}

test('ROW-121-caret-focus-selection-scroll-copy-and-soft-keyboard-leave-the-check-in-place', async ({ page }) => {
  asActor('anonymous');
  const rng = freshRandom();
  const { text, shown } = await longChecked(page, rng, 'ROW-121');
  const count = (await readCount(page)).text;
  const offer = el(page, ROLES.offer).first();

  const unchanged = async (after: string) => {
    await settle(page);
    expect(await listed(page, text), `ROW-121: after ${after}, every highlight is still in place (seed ${rng.seed})`).toEqual(shown);
    expect((await readCount(page)).text, `ROW-121: after ${after}, the count line is unchanged`).toBe(count);
    expect(await readOfferText(page), `ROW-121: after ${after}, the text is unchanged`).toBe(text);
  };

  await offer.focus();
  for (const k of ['ArrowLeft', 'ArrowRight', 'ArrowDown', 'ArrowUp', 'Home', 'End', 'ControlOrMeta+Home']) await page.keyboard.press(k);
  await unchanged('caret moves (arrows, Home, End, Ctrl/Cmd+Home)');

  for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) await page.keyboard.press('Shift+ArrowRight');
  await page.keyboard.press('ControlOrMeta+A');
  await unchanged('selection (Shift+arrows, Ctrl/Cmd+A)');

  await page.keyboard.press('ControlOrMeta+C');
  await unchanged('copying (Ctrl/Cmd+C)');

  await page.keyboard.press('Tab');
  await page.keyboard.press('Shift+Tab');
  await unchanged('focus leaving and returning (Tab, Shift+Tab)');

  const box = await offer.boundingBox();
  if (box) await page.mouse.move(box.x + box.width / 2, box.y + Math.min(box.height / 2, 40));
  await page.mouse.wheel(0, 600);
  await settle(page);
  await page.mouse.wheel(0, -600);
  await unchanged('scrolling (mouse wheel down and up)');

  const size = page.viewportSize();
  if (!size) throw new Error('setup: the page has no viewport size to shrink');
  if (await isTouch(page)) await offer.tap();
  else await offer.focus();
  await page.setViewportSize({ width: size.width, height: Math.max(200, size.height - 300) });
  await settle(page);
  await page.setViewportSize(size);
  await unchanged('the soft keyboard opening and closing (focus, viewport shrunk by its height, restored)');

  await typeAtEnd(page, 'y');
  await expect.poll(() => listed(page, text + 'y'), { message: 'ROW-121: a change of the text does clear them', timeout: WAIT_MS }).toEqual([]);
});

test('ROW-121-control-the-long-text-check-shows-highlights-and-the-count', async ({ page }) => {
  asActor('anonymous');
  await longChecked(page, freshRandom(), 'ROW-121 control');
});
